# T13 — Repo resolution, burst grouping, context gathering: COMPLETE

## Files owned and changed
- `test/slack-context.test.ts` (new): failing-first tests for T13 —
  URL beats channel default; no repo → ask with `startRun: false`;
  20-message single-author burst yields one run; different author,
  window expiry, and 20-msg/100KB bounds split bursts; `aside`
  excluded; mute/unmute gating; pasted token redacted; 400-message
  thread capped at ~50; linked issue/PR text included.
- `src/slack-context.ts` (new): `extractGitHubRepoUrl`,
  `parseChannelRepoMap`, `resolveSlackRepo` (mention URL → thread URL
  → channel map → ask, never guess), `clampBurstWindowSeconds`
  (1–300s, default 10s), `groupMessageBursts` (sliding window /
  author change / 20 msgs / 100KB → one run per burst),
  `applyThreadControls` (`aside` excluded, mute/unmute), and
  `gatherSlackContext` (aside-filtered, last-50 capped, `boundTail`
  per body, linked texts appended, `redactSecrets` over assembly).

## TDD evidence
- BEFORE implement: `npx vitest run test/slack-context.test.ts` → FAIL
  (Cannot find module '../src/slack-context.js').
- AFTER implement: `npx vitest run test/slack-context.test.ts` → PASS (18 passed).
- `npx vitest run test/slack.test.ts test/slack-context.test.ts` → PASS (26 passed).
- `npx tsc --noEmit` → no errors in slack-context files
  (repo-wide failures are other agents' uncommitted work, untouched).
- `npx eslint src/slack-context.ts test/slack-context.test.ts` → clean.

